# Where "Open The App" points while developing.
#
# apps/web runs on Vite's default port and hash-routes, so the product's opening
# screen is #/case - the worked example, not the About tab, because someone
# arriving from the landing page has just read what the thing is.
#
# Committed on purpose: it holds no secret, and without it `npm run landing:dev`
# links to /app/, which does not exist on the dev server.
# QUOTED, and it has to be: dotenv treats an unquoted `#` as the start of a
# comment, so the bare form silently loses the `#/case` fragment and the button
# lands on the app's default route instead of the worked example.
VITE_APP_URL="http://localhost:5173/#/case"
